[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106649,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Bizarre parosteal osteochondromatous proliferation (BPOP) is a benign lesion of the bone surface, composed of an admixture of cartilage, bone, and spindle cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106650,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9212/0 Bizarre parosteal osteochondromatous proliferation</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106651,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E82.Z &amp; XH23J5 Benign chondrogenic tumours, site unspecified &amp; Bizarre parosteal osteochondromatous proliferation</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106652,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> Nora lesion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106653,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106654,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Small bones of the distal extremities (mainly the metacarpals and middle phalanges) are affected, with hands four times more commonly affected than feet {32611484}. Involvement of distal phalanges is uncommon. Long tubular bones may be affected {8317609}. Craniofacial bone involvement has been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106655,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients typically present with a painless mass of a few months&rsquo; to several years&rsquo; duration. Pain and rapid growth have been reported {21533526}. Radiologically, BPOP is a well-marginated ossified mass arising from the cortical bone without periosteal reaction, flaring of the underlying cortex, or corticomedullary continuity with affected bone. Exceptional cases may show corticomedullary continuity {17437102}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106656,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>BPOP has a wide age distribution. Most patients are in their third or fourth decade of life, and there is no sex predilection {15252309}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106657,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "<p>A history of trauma is reported in a subset of patients {8317609}, and it has been hypothesized by some that BPOP is part of a spectrum encompassing reactive processes, including fibro-osseous tumour of digits and turret exostosis. However, the presence of recurrent cytogenetic abnormalities in some cases suggests that it is a neoplastic process.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-17T14:53:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106658,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrent cytogenetic abnormalities, including t(1;17)(q32;q21), inv(7)(q22q32), and inv(6)(p25q15), have been reported {15343507; 15926071; 22075515; 21509435; 24412018}, suggesting that BPOP is a neoplastic process.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106659,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>BPOP is an exophytic bony lesion with a cartilaginous surface, usually measuring 10&ndash;30&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106660,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>BPOP is composed of three distinct components with varying degrees of representation: (1)&nbsp;hypercellular cartilage containing frequently enlarged, bizarre, binucleated chondrocytes; (2)&nbsp;cancellous bone undergoing maturation via enchondral ossification, with calcified cartilage having a characteristic basophilic tinctorial quality (known as blue bone); and (3)&nbsp;spindle cell stroma without cytological atypia. Myxoid and fibrocartilaginous tissue may be seen. Atypical mitoses are not seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106661,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106662,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106663,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> an exophytic bone lesion composed of disorganized, hypercellular cartilage containing atypical chondrocytes, spindle cells, and bone (including characteristic blue bone).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106664,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106665,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 202,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>BPOP is a benign lesion, with no capacity to metastasize. It is treated with simple excision. Recurrences occur in approximately 50% of cases and are managed by re-excision.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:17:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]